WEBVTT

00:06.047 --> 00:08.049
[theme music playing]

01:03.313 --> 01:05.982
GENIE, MAKE A WISH

01:06.983 --> 01:08.276
[in Mongolian] My name is Hunbish.

01:11.279 --> 01:15.075
-[growling softly]
-What did you see last night?

01:31.800 --> 01:35.345
[Wahid in Korean]
Shadi brought me out of the ring.

01:37.180 --> 01:38.973
-[Shadi grunts]
-[pulsating]

01:40.934 --> 01:42.268
[in Arabic] Run away.

01:44.062 --> 01:44.938
[breath trembles]

01:47.941 --> 01:51.027
[Wahid in Korean]
The entire world was fast asleep.

01:51.569 --> 01:52.695
[guard grunts softly]

01:53.446 --> 01:58.243
As he left, Shadi tugged a single thread
from the rug in Father's room.

01:58.326 --> 02:01.162
-[guard grunting softly]
-He told me

02:01.246 --> 02:02.789
to run away.

02:09.754 --> 02:11.047
What did you use my thread for?

02:12.632 --> 02:14.717
You put the world to sleep
without permission?

02:17.095 --> 02:18.304
Tisah.

02:18.388 --> 02:20.557
[tense music playing]

02:25.770 --> 02:27.355
-[squelching]
-[gasps]

02:29.357 --> 02:32.652
[gurgling]

02:37.740 --> 02:40.743
[retching, coughing]

02:42.370 --> 02:44.205
[Hunbish] What did you
find out yesterday?

02:44.706 --> 02:46.457
A way to release those shackles?

02:46.958 --> 02:49.711
Or someone to release them for you?

02:51.629 --> 02:53.590
[in Arabic] When Iblis woke up,

02:53.673 --> 02:55.341
he would've known I'd been there.

02:56.092 --> 02:57.218
[apple thuds]

02:57.302 --> 02:59.387
Ah. So you found hope?

02:59.470 --> 03:02.891
Hope that your brother
will come and save you?

03:03.808 --> 03:07.061
Has it really never occurred to you

03:07.562 --> 03:10.064
that if I didn't want you
putting the world to sleep,

03:10.148 --> 03:13.067
I would have tied your tongue
and not your feet?

03:13.151 --> 03:15.153
[dramatic music plays]

03:16.529 --> 03:17.906
I was also curious to know

03:17.989 --> 03:23.036
if that bitch would be able
to cut my thread in this life as well.

03:23.119 --> 03:26.706
So I had been patiently waiting
for you to have a little outing.

03:30.126 --> 03:33.129
[chuckles, in Korean] Thanks to you,
I finally have my answer.

03:33.212 --> 03:35.548
[in Arabic]
You're still set on this, Khalid?

03:36.090 --> 03:37.175
Please stop.

03:37.258 --> 03:38.843
Or my brother will kill you.

03:38.927 --> 03:40.261
[in Korean] Why would I die?

03:40.345 --> 03:42.805
If I can just make that lamp my own…

03:43.514 --> 03:45.558
Once I become the master of that lamp,

03:46.643 --> 03:49.479
I'll be the only being
who can cut my threads,

03:50.271 --> 03:53.566
which would mean
I can become the leader of all spirits!

04:00.240 --> 04:01.282
Who is Khalid?

04:01.366 --> 04:02.492
You scared me!

04:02.575 --> 04:03.952
Why are you still here?

04:05.119 --> 04:06.204
Why am I still here?

04:06.287 --> 04:10.083
You all just bolted out.
How exactly was I supposed to get out?

04:10.166 --> 04:11.292
[Iblis] Right.

04:11.376 --> 04:13.711
Wait, isn't that heavy?

04:16.547 --> 04:18.174
I asked you who Khalid is.

04:19.217 --> 04:21.761
Khalid? I'm not sure. Who's that?

04:21.844 --> 04:23.179
You would know, not me!

04:23.263 --> 04:26.349
All of this happened
because you locked me up in here!

04:26.432 --> 04:27.684
Cut the crap.

04:27.767 --> 04:28.851
I saw for myself,

04:28.935 --> 04:31.896
and you'd have been locked up
even if it weren't for me, Satan!

04:31.980 --> 04:36.526
That deity of yours was just using me
as a durability test for his creations.

04:38.027 --> 04:40.822
You're right about that. [chuckling]

04:41.698 --> 04:43.324
I'll let it slide since you agreed.

04:46.619 --> 04:49.956
[sighs] I saw the sand was flowing,
so I touched it.

04:50.790 --> 04:52.208
Then I suddenly saw it.

04:52.292 --> 04:54.377
Hmm? What did you see?

04:58.506 --> 05:00.883
[Ka-young] In what seemed like
the distant past,

05:00.967 --> 05:03.720
there was a boy weaving a rug in the sun.

05:04.887 --> 05:06.556
And I was there beside him.

05:07.056 --> 05:08.850
I called his name.

05:08.933 --> 05:10.268
-[in Arabic] Khalid.
-[thuds softly]

05:14.147 --> 05:14.981
[in Korean] Are you sure?

05:15.064 --> 05:18.151
I'm sure.
I was just as pretty as I am now.

05:22.905 --> 05:24.866
For starters, get me out of here.

05:25.867 --> 05:27.618
Hey! [sighs]

05:28.202 --> 05:30.038
You're getting it everywhere.

05:37.086 --> 05:38.880
Grandma. Try shaking your arm.

05:39.714 --> 05:40.715
Is it heavy?

05:41.716 --> 05:43.760
This teeny thing? What is this?

05:43.843 --> 05:45.219
Is this what's trendy now?

05:45.303 --> 05:47.555
Oh Pan-geum, try breaking the thread.

05:47.638 --> 05:49.640
You want me to break it? Like this?

05:50.141 --> 05:52.143
-Mm?
-It breaks.

05:52.226 --> 05:54.729
It doesn't work between humans.

05:56.355 --> 05:57.190
Tie me with it.

05:57.273 --> 05:59.776
[sighs] You should brace yourself.

05:59.859 --> 06:02.945
I'm a spirit, so I have… [grunts, strains]

06:03.029 --> 06:07.116
I have infinite magic… [groaning]

06:07.742 --> 06:09.744
[straining]

06:09.827 --> 06:12.413
[sighs in relief] There you go.

06:12.497 --> 06:13.623
You apparently don't.

06:14.373 --> 06:15.583
[thread snaps]

06:15.666 --> 06:18.336
It doesn't work
from spirits to humans either.

06:19.462 --> 06:20.463
Now tie yourself up.

06:20.546 --> 06:21.464
What?

06:22.632 --> 06:25.218
Right, well… [chuckles nervously]

06:25.301 --> 06:26.469
…you know,

06:26.552 --> 06:28.888
you can never rule out chance,
and I don't want to--

06:28.971 --> 06:30.640
-Do it.
-I'm doing it.

06:31.140 --> 06:33.434
-[foot thuds]
-[groans, grunts]

06:34.393 --> 06:37.146
[Iblis grunting]

06:37.230 --> 06:40.775
[grunts] It's done. Now break it.

06:41.567 --> 06:42.610
Please?

06:43.694 --> 06:45.446
Grandma, try breaking the thread.

06:45.530 --> 06:48.407
Goodness me.
What is this, some kind of mutt training?

06:48.491 --> 06:50.910
Gosh. [exhales]

06:55.957 --> 06:59.794
What the… It broke so easily before.
[inhales sharply]

06:59.877 --> 07:01.379
-Wait here.
-Wait!

07:01.462 --> 07:03.297
[Mi-ju] Let's see. Yes, these.

07:03.381 --> 07:04.549
[scissors snipping]

07:04.632 --> 07:05.591
[Iblis] Okay.

07:06.300 --> 07:08.302
-Great.
-[Mi-ju breathes deeply]

07:10.596 --> 07:11.848
What is this?

07:13.808 --> 07:15.101
Wait right here.

07:15.601 --> 07:18.646
-The straw cutter will be in the shed.
-Are you sure you even tried?

07:19.981 --> 07:22.984
It only works
when a spirit ties another spirit.

07:23.067 --> 07:25.653
-That's the thread's rule.
-Okay, I get it.

07:26.279 --> 07:27.947
Just break it already. [chuckles]

07:28.030 --> 07:29.615
[Sade] By the way… [snorts]

07:29.699 --> 07:30.950
…that thread reeks of blood.

07:31.534 --> 07:33.536
-What?
-Blood?

07:41.461 --> 07:43.004
So it was originally white.

07:43.087 --> 07:45.047
It looks black because it's bloodstained.

07:45.131 --> 07:48.468
Given the information we have
and the fact that I can cut it,

07:48.551 --> 07:50.094
this must be my blood.

07:50.178 --> 07:53.264
[gasps] That's shocking.
Try breaking it already.

07:53.347 --> 07:55.433
Let's take a detailed,
thorough look at it.

07:56.767 --> 07:59.687
[sighs] About how you left me out to dry.

07:59.770 --> 08:01.606
The grains of my ashes were very fine.

08:01.689 --> 08:04.150
You must have taken extra care
to air me out real good.

08:04.650 --> 08:07.403
Grandma! Haven't you found
the straw cutter yet?

08:07.487 --> 08:09.447
-Hey.
-We should grab the big cutter!

08:09.530 --> 08:10.781
Hey, Master!

08:11.824 --> 08:14.285
[grunts] Wait, just get this…

08:17.205 --> 08:18.581
Quit stuffing your face, jerk.

08:19.624 --> 08:21.751
[gulps, exhales]

08:22.335 --> 08:24.712
[retching]

08:24.795 --> 08:27.131
[coughing]

08:30.593 --> 08:31.719
[exhales]

08:33.304 --> 08:34.847
Are you going to stay in here?

08:37.099 --> 08:38.100
What's with you guys?

08:38.184 --> 08:41.479
You, for one, and everyone else
in the front yard. Who are you?

08:42.063 --> 08:44.065
How is Hun your father?

08:44.148 --> 08:47.193
Enough to pay off your debts
and gamble to your heart's content.

08:47.276 --> 08:48.736
You said that's all you needed.

08:49.487 --> 08:51.614
So why are you asking questions now?

08:51.697 --> 08:55.284
I didn't know I was getting into something
with lives at stake!

08:55.868 --> 08:57.078
[breath trembling]

08:58.037 --> 08:59.497
I can't afford to make mistakes.

09:01.082 --> 09:02.583
I'm his dad, after all.

09:10.633 --> 09:13.219
Why the hell are you all so helpless
against a damn kid?

09:13.302 --> 09:14.554
[laughs incredulously]

09:16.430 --> 09:17.640
You're asking that too.

09:18.808 --> 09:21.644
Father's previous parents
all asked the same question.

09:22.603 --> 09:26.440
You know something? To orphans,
the entire world is nothing but horror.

09:26.941 --> 09:29.485
[child 1 screaming, wailing]

09:42.123 --> 09:44.709
[Wahid] But if you've lived
the greatest horror of all,

09:46.419 --> 09:48.421
everything else pales by comparison.

09:48.504 --> 09:50.172
[child 2 screaming]

09:58.431 --> 10:00.725
[screaming]

10:02.935 --> 10:06.272
[Wahid] The weak get torn apart,
and the strong are rewarded with meat.

10:06.772 --> 10:09.400
That's all we need.

10:20.953 --> 10:23.789
[gags, retches]

10:23.873 --> 10:25.625
[Wahid] So don't bother trying so hard.

10:25.708 --> 10:28.252
No matter what you do,
we'll only listen to Father.

10:28.336 --> 10:30.463
This bullshit ends today.

10:30.546 --> 10:33.299
Tomorrow, we're getting you
some hiking gear.

10:33.382 --> 10:34.925
[Jun-u coughing]

10:35.009 --> 10:38.012
[door opens, closes]

10:40.473 --> 10:42.475
[pop music playing over speakers]

10:44.560 --> 10:46.103
[Mi-ju sighs]

10:48.356 --> 10:52.026
[sighs] I keep getting
stuck here. [scoffs]

10:52.109 --> 10:55.321
[winces] Gosh, beauty really is pain.

10:56.280 --> 10:58.282
-[Min-ji] Are you getting an extra shot?
-[gasps]

10:58.366 --> 10:59.742
I won't ask anything else.

10:59.825 --> 11:01.661
Just whether you want an extra shot.

11:03.329 --> 11:04.914
Extra shot, please.

11:04.997 --> 11:07.958
[Min-ji] What about whipped cream?
And caramel syrup?

11:08.584 --> 11:11.379
[sighs] More questions. Silly me.

11:11.879 --> 11:14.840
I could just add everything
to make it tasty.

11:15.466 --> 11:16.592
[giggling]

11:21.263 --> 11:22.932
I wasn't trying to be funny.

11:24.350 --> 11:26.644
This isn't a question.
I'm just jumping to conclusions,

11:26.727 --> 11:28.145
so you don't have to answer.

11:29.105 --> 11:30.689
-Oh.
-[plastic crinkles]

11:30.773 --> 11:31.816
Is your name Lee Mi-ju?

11:33.192 --> 11:34.026
It's fake, right?

11:35.069 --> 11:36.779
And you're not Lee Beul-li's sister.

11:41.117 --> 11:44.620
[sighs] I'd really like an answer
to this one though.

11:45.162 --> 11:49.375
Are you being hunted by the government
or taking on the whole country?

11:49.458 --> 11:52.962
Gosh, how could you say such a thing?
It's absolutely not that!

11:55.089 --> 11:55.965
Good, then.

11:56.715 --> 11:58.592
And this is just to reassure you.

11:58.676 --> 11:59.885
Ka-young

12:00.594 --> 12:02.012
is as good as they come.

12:02.930 --> 12:07.184
I just mean you should ignore
whatever you hear others saying about her.

12:09.145 --> 12:11.397
[sighs] My goodness.

12:12.231 --> 12:14.525
[breath trembling]
Goodness, I'm so grateful.

12:16.527 --> 12:18.863
-Wait, you're tearing up?
-[chuckles softly]

12:20.406 --> 12:21.490
[sniffles]

12:22.867 --> 12:25.077
-[gentle music plays]
-[chuckles dreamily]

12:32.501 --> 12:34.086
What's with the cherry blossoms?

12:36.088 --> 12:37.965
Is this even the right season for that?

12:41.385 --> 12:42.386
[Min-ji chuckles softly]

12:44.847 --> 12:47.808
[Yeong-hyeon] All right, everyone.
I'll show you everything. Through here--

12:47.892 --> 12:49.226
[man] Sir, we can't let you pass.

12:49.310 --> 12:52.605
[Yeong-hyeon] Didn't you hear that I was
the first to discover it and call it in?

12:52.688 --> 12:53.731
I'll take a quick peek.

12:53.814 --> 12:56.859
Everyone says that,
based on the diameter of the pelvis found,

12:56.942 --> 12:59.111
the corpse is most likely female.

12:59.195 --> 13:01.197
Apparently, she originally had red hair,

13:01.280 --> 13:04.658
-but it was dyed after she was killed!
-[snickering]

13:05.284 --> 13:08.245
That means this is a very serious crime.

13:08.329 --> 13:10.164
And who discovered it?

13:20.508 --> 13:21.425
Ms. Ki?

13:22.468 --> 13:24.595
What brings you here, Ms. Ki?

13:25.846 --> 13:29.183
This was stuck in your tail light
when you left your car with me.

13:29.934 --> 13:32.561
What on earth do you mean?

13:33.062 --> 13:34.772
What is this?

13:34.855 --> 13:36.524
Take a look and see for yourself.

13:37.066 --> 13:40.611
To me, it looks like a woman's
bleached blonde hair.

13:40.694 --> 13:43.697
[tense music playing]

13:47.493 --> 13:48.494
Why give me this?

13:49.537 --> 13:51.247
I don't understand.

13:51.747 --> 13:52.873
What's going on here?

13:52.957 --> 13:54.750
Your face tells me you do understand.

13:54.833 --> 13:56.835
You're behind it, aren't you?

13:57.336 --> 13:58.837
The skeleton they found.

13:59.380 --> 14:02.216
And I'm guessing you did the same
to the owner of that hair.

14:02.716 --> 14:03.676
Ms. Ki.

14:04.260 --> 14:07.263
Someone might seriously get
the wrong idea if they heard you.

14:09.223 --> 14:10.057
By the way…

14:12.601 --> 14:13.769
did you come alone?

14:14.353 --> 14:15.229
Of course not.

14:15.938 --> 14:17.940
I'm here with someone
you'd never dream of.

14:31.036 --> 14:33.289
Don't waste my time and listen up.

14:34.373 --> 14:37.042
The police are looking for this woman.
Look familiar?

14:37.126 --> 14:38.836
She has the same hair color too.

14:39.879 --> 14:42.214
I actually looked
in your truck bed that day.

14:42.298 --> 14:45.009
Everything else made sense,
but one thing felt out of place.

14:46.719 --> 14:47.720
BLACK HAIR DYE

14:47.803 --> 14:49.305
And then I saw the news.

14:49.388 --> 14:52.349
Oh, he dyes their hair
after their death. How fun.

14:53.642 --> 14:55.185
You think that's fun?

14:56.478 --> 14:58.814
Well, every masterpiece needs a signature.

15:01.066 --> 15:03.485
That's why I came. To give you a gift.

15:03.986 --> 15:04.820
Here.

15:11.660 --> 15:13.454
You're actually giving me this

15:13.954 --> 15:17.082
instead of taking it to the cops?

15:18.375 --> 15:19.209
Why?

15:23.297 --> 15:25.549
-[man 1 farts]
-[all snickering]

15:26.842 --> 15:29.178
[man 2] I guess someone's
digestive system is working well.

15:29.678 --> 15:32.598
-You should finish up.
-[all laughing]

15:32.681 --> 15:36.310
-[man 1 farting]
-[man 2] Come on, not that.

15:36.894 --> 15:40.522
-Finish up the bowing.
-[all laughing]

15:41.482 --> 15:44.526
The same reason you had me
fix your tail light, I suppose.

15:45.027 --> 15:46.737
Because you and I are alike.

15:46.820 --> 15:48.364
[tense music continues]

15:48.447 --> 15:50.324
[cackling]

15:52.451 --> 15:53.744
I knew it.

15:53.827 --> 15:55.454
I knew you'd be just like me!

15:55.537 --> 15:57.539
No. Unlike you, I'd never make a mistake.

15:58.707 --> 16:02.753
If only there were a way
for you to fix that error.

16:02.836 --> 16:05.839
Uh, there is a way.
Don't worry about that.

16:05.923 --> 16:09.051
If this all works out well,
why don't we do the next one together?

16:09.134 --> 16:10.719
Let's talk after you fix it.

16:11.845 --> 16:13.347
I don't work with amateurs.

16:16.100 --> 16:16.934
[Sang-Tae chuckles]

16:20.562 --> 16:22.856
[eerie music intensifies, stops]

16:29.738 --> 16:32.908
Why did you do that?
Why did you give the culprit the evidence?

16:34.284 --> 16:37.079
He's the only one who knows
where the missing woman is buried.

16:38.247 --> 16:40.666
If I took that to the cops
and they caught him,

16:41.583 --> 16:43.919
then that bastard
would use his last wish to escape.

16:44.003 --> 16:45.629
That woman would be lost forever.

16:45.713 --> 16:48.674
That's why I made it
so he'd make his third wish sooner.

16:48.757 --> 16:53.345
Ah. I don't think I'm the one who
should be taking on the immortal being.

16:53.429 --> 16:58.142
Eom Sang-tae will surely want to go
back in time to get rid of the evidence.

16:58.642 --> 17:00.477
When Eom Sang-tae makes his final wish,

17:01.061 --> 17:02.813
give my notebook to my past self.

17:02.896 --> 17:04.064
Why should I?

17:04.148 --> 17:06.358
Let's make it clear.
I only fulfill wishes--

17:06.442 --> 17:09.403
You're a big fat liar.
The writing on the bottom of the lamp.

17:10.779 --> 17:12.781
The translation says
it's the date it was made.

17:13.282 --> 17:14.408
You translated it?

17:14.491 --> 17:17.453
It says it was made in the year 1061.
Haven't you seen it?

17:17.536 --> 17:19.288
Do you check beneath your floors?

17:24.460 --> 17:25.669
OCTOBER 24, 1061

17:25.753 --> 17:26.962
You're right.

17:27.046 --> 17:30.799
Did you not harp on about being locked up
for 983 years because of me?

17:30.883 --> 17:32.384
But you're off by 20 years.

17:32.468 --> 17:35.262
Did you goof around for 20 years
and then get locked up?

17:35.345 --> 17:36.346
I'm sure I didn't!

17:36.430 --> 17:39.016
I counted every single year
with extra precision…

17:39.850 --> 17:41.518
Or so I thought… so what's this?

17:41.602 --> 17:43.937
Master. I found the smell.

17:44.021 --> 17:44.980
Right.

17:45.564 --> 17:46.565
What smell?

17:46.648 --> 17:48.734
I've been doing my own investigation.

17:53.530 --> 17:55.532
[ominous music playing]

17:59.203 --> 18:02.039
It's actually a little different
from the original scent,

18:02.122 --> 18:03.624
but not completely.

18:04.124 --> 18:06.376
I'm not sure why, but either way,

18:06.877 --> 18:09.213
the immortal one's scent
is coming from that house.

18:14.426 --> 18:16.637
It seems Shadi is here too.

18:22.142 --> 18:24.436
-[whirring stops]
-You want us to visit Dubai?

18:24.937 --> 18:25.771
Why?

18:25.854 --> 18:29.691
I have a brother in Dubai who'd know
what went down when I was locked up.

18:30.192 --> 18:32.945
But we don't know when
Eom Sang-tae will make his final wish.

18:33.946 --> 18:36.657
I can come, wherever I am.
And the notebook is in the lamp.

18:38.242 --> 18:39.535
I guess you're right.

18:40.702 --> 18:42.121
But why should I go?

18:43.330 --> 18:45.040
Because I'd be safest by your side?

18:46.041 --> 18:48.293
No. Because I'd be safest by your side.

18:49.128 --> 18:51.880
What if I get tied up again? [laughing]

18:55.843 --> 18:56.802
[sighs]

19:02.766 --> 19:04.351
I was a little careless, wasn't I?

19:06.854 --> 19:08.522
[Min-ji] What a motley crew.

19:10.524 --> 19:13.026
I see. Is this one
finally being kicked out?

19:14.194 --> 19:15.028
In your dreams.

19:16.196 --> 19:18.615
I'm pretty sure I only asked you to come.

19:19.241 --> 19:21.994
The people who are safest by my side
need to come with us.

19:22.995 --> 19:25.330
I've got things to take care of there,
so I need you

19:25.914 --> 19:27.541
to take good care of Mi-ju for me.

19:27.624 --> 19:29.543
She's never been abroad before.

19:29.626 --> 19:32.045
Didn't you say these two were siblings?

19:32.129 --> 19:34.214
-Now this is her first trip to Dubai?
-[gasps]

19:35.549 --> 19:37.551
-We're new siblings.
-We're new siblings. Huh.

19:39.011 --> 19:42.764
[sighs] Whether you're siblings
or sisters, we're headed to Dubai.

19:42.848 --> 19:44.558
And the tickets are first class.

19:44.641 --> 19:45.642
[in English] Let's go.

19:46.685 --> 19:47.936
[chuckles]

19:51.481 --> 19:53.692
[romantic music plays]

20:11.793 --> 20:13.795
[upbeat pop music playing]

20:25.599 --> 20:28.685
Mm! Ah!

20:32.314 --> 20:34.024
[Mi-ju squeals]

20:35.192 --> 20:36.652
Oh. Ah.

20:37.277 --> 20:39.071
[man speaking in English] Thank you.

20:39.154 --> 20:42.157
[Min-ji in Korean]
Ah. You're cute from every angle.

20:42.241 --> 20:45.118
How did you get here, exactly?
I didn't see you in first class.

20:45.202 --> 20:47.955
How? I got here by something else. A lam--

20:48.038 --> 20:49.331
[shushes]

20:50.249 --> 20:52.125
Yeah, okay. Who cares how you got here?

20:52.626 --> 20:54.795
And we're getting picked up
in a limo, no less.

20:54.878 --> 20:58.340
For starters,
let's take the limo to the hotel and eat.

20:58.423 --> 21:00.092
Eat as much as you want, Min-ji.

21:01.343 --> 21:03.178
We'll head to Old Dubai first.

21:03.679 --> 21:04.680
Why there?

21:05.555 --> 21:07.599
[music playing faintly over speakers]

21:17.651 --> 21:21.071
-Mm. See that jar here?
-What?

21:21.154 --> 21:23.699
-You want me to buy it for you?
-[tuts] No.

21:24.366 --> 21:25.659
Could you rub it for me?

21:26.660 --> 21:28.287
If I do it, no one will come.

21:30.831 --> 21:33.250
[chiming]

21:35.711 --> 21:37.713
[magical music plays]

21:49.182 --> 21:51.310
-[gasps]
-Song Hye-kyo!

21:51.393 --> 21:52.311
[Iblis] Huh?

21:53.103 --> 21:53.937
Is that you?

21:54.021 --> 21:55.689
Is this a famous face?

21:56.231 --> 21:58.025
You rubbed my jar so vigorously

21:58.108 --> 22:01.653
that I just chose a face I liked
from your region on Netflix.

22:04.865 --> 22:07.117
[sighs, in Arabic] You set me up?

22:08.118 --> 22:09.578
-Piss off.
-[scoffs]

22:10.579 --> 22:12.873
[in Korean] Do you happen
to be a genie too?

22:14.750 --> 22:16.752
You made her rub it
without an explanation?

22:18.045 --> 22:20.047
Me? I'm his ex-girlfriend.

22:21.048 --> 22:24.968
-Oh, Jinniya?
-Huh? Hmm.

22:25.719 --> 22:28.764
It's been a really long time, hasn't it?

22:29.348 --> 22:31.058
Could we chat for a moment?

22:31.141 --> 22:33.810
A moment? Given our past,
would a moment really be enough?

22:34.770 --> 22:37.481
Hand over the coffee cup set
I bought for you in the BC era.

22:39.691 --> 22:41.693
[gasps, whines]

22:45.989 --> 22:48.408
I wouldn't still have that.
I bet it's a relic by now.

22:48.492 --> 22:51.203
Then what about the rug I gave you?
At least give that back.

22:52.621 --> 22:55.373
[Iblis] That too.
It got worn out over time.

22:55.457 --> 22:58.293
It probably helped date palms
grow tall and strong.

22:58.376 --> 22:59.586
Well then,

22:59.669 --> 23:01.463
enjoy your chat.

23:02.130 --> 23:05.383
-I'll see you later. You're dead meat.
-[sighs]

23:06.176 --> 23:09.012
-Wait, you're that bitch from back then.
-Huh?

23:09.096 --> 23:13.600
Ah. And you're a bitch who also knows me?
Where I'm from, reincarnation is a thing.

23:14.976 --> 23:19.272
[scoffs] We just met,
and she's calling me a bitch?

23:19.356 --> 23:20.482
[Iblis] Hey.

23:21.024 --> 23:23.276
Do you think we could go
to your jar for now?

23:24.111 --> 23:25.570
Do you think I'm insane?

23:25.654 --> 23:28.156
[sighs] I must be insane

23:28.740 --> 23:30.367
to let you back in here.

23:30.909 --> 23:34.788
I guess the interior is
a lot more understated now.

23:35.539 --> 23:37.249
Time sure is a cruel mistress.

23:37.332 --> 23:39.292
Just spit it out. What? What is it?

23:39.376 --> 23:40.794
Why have you come to see me?

23:41.670 --> 23:43.171
I just have two quick questions.

23:43.255 --> 23:47.467
Have you ever taken on
a different appearance just to trick me?

23:48.051 --> 23:50.178
Like you did today.

23:50.262 --> 23:53.974
Did you ever take on the face
of the human woman you just saw

23:54.474 --> 23:58.270
and, you know,
smile widely and prettily at me?

23:58.353 --> 24:01.356
Get out. And would you just die already?

24:01.940 --> 24:03.900
It really wasn't you? Ah.

24:04.651 --> 24:05.485
Okay, then.

24:05.569 --> 24:08.822
Do you remember our brother,
the one who controlled sleep?

24:10.323 --> 24:11.158
Shadi?

24:11.241 --> 24:12.617
-Yes.
-What about him?

24:13.201 --> 24:15.287
I haven't seen him in about 600 years.

24:15.370 --> 24:18.874
He put me to sleep and left me tied up
with thread that's impossible to break.

24:18.957 --> 24:20.333
Know anything about that?

24:21.168 --> 24:23.003
The thread was unbreakable?

24:24.671 --> 24:28.925
Shadi had a son with a human woman.

24:29.009 --> 24:30.635
He wove rugs.

24:31.720 --> 24:33.221
But the boy died.

24:33.305 --> 24:36.766
He was half human and half spirit,
so he lived a mortal life.

24:38.018 --> 24:40.520
Shadi had a son?

24:40.604 --> 24:43.440
-[door opens]
-[footsteps approaching]

24:44.316 --> 24:46.818
[somber music playing]

24:49.738 --> 24:54.159
Now Shadi can only sing
when you desire, Father.

24:55.785 --> 24:57.329
Back at the festival that time,

24:57.913 --> 24:59.581
I saw Iblis.

24:59.664 --> 25:01.666
[indistinct conversation]

25:07.589 --> 25:12.594
[in deep voice, Arabic] He had
the same face he wore 963 years ago.

25:12.677 --> 25:16.056
[Shadi] If my brother wants to hide,
you'll never recognize him.

25:16.139 --> 25:21.686
I may not recognize him,
but you most certainly would.

25:22.354 --> 25:25.273
[in normal voice, Korean] If I eliminate
the lamp's master… [metal clanks]

25:25.357 --> 25:28.109
…you will bring me Iblis's lamp,
won't you?

25:29.110 --> 25:30.195
[sighs]

25:38.870 --> 25:41.248
[Iblis] Was his son's name Khalid
by any chance?

25:43.458 --> 25:44.709
I wouldn't know his name.

25:45.877 --> 25:49.756
In any case, after all that fuss,
you seriously sought her out again?

25:49.839 --> 25:52.342
I didn't seek her out.
She was reborn and found my lamp…

25:52.425 --> 25:53.426
Wait.

25:54.386 --> 25:55.345
Hold up.

25:56.846 --> 26:00.016
How come you recognize Ki Ka-young?
She died at eight in her past life.

26:00.100 --> 26:01.726
What are you talking about?

26:01.810 --> 26:04.020
Because of her,
you took an entire city, and…

26:05.313 --> 26:06.564
Damn it.

26:07.065 --> 26:08.900
This must be the 20 years he sealed.

26:10.277 --> 26:12.279
Hey, get lost already.

26:12.779 --> 26:15.407
You and I never met, all right?

26:16.283 --> 26:18.410
Hey, wait. What does that even mean?

26:22.122 --> 26:23.915
Huh? My memories were sealed?

26:23.999 --> 26:26.001
[laughing]

26:26.084 --> 26:27.168
Huh?

26:28.712 --> 26:29.629
But…

26:30.672 --> 26:32.549
[tense music playing]

26:53.611 --> 26:55.155
[Ejllael in Arabic] Nice look, Zahara.

26:55.655 --> 26:58.616
Where are all those countless
beautiful flowers of yours?

26:59.576 --> 27:03.580
This is the only flower left.
The immortal's one.

27:09.544 --> 27:10.462
[snickers]

27:13.089 --> 27:14.341
Anyway,

27:15.300 --> 27:17.761
have you heard that Iblis got out?

27:20.513 --> 27:22.682
Has Iblis's punishment ended?

27:23.558 --> 27:24.601
Where is he now?

27:26.686 --> 27:28.938
All of your brothers
are in the land of Goryeo.

27:29.022 --> 27:31.524
Even Shadi is there, getting on my nerves.

27:32.317 --> 27:36.363
[sighs] Anyway, Iblis may pay you a visit
very soon.

27:36.446 --> 27:37.697
So keep your mouth shut.

27:39.407 --> 27:42.369
No matter what Iblis asks,
do not reveal what you remember.

27:42.452 --> 27:44.704
[tense music continues playing]

27:47.332 --> 27:49.667
You remember your grave mistake,

27:50.377 --> 27:51.336
don't you?

27:55.590 --> 27:57.550
[music intensifies, fades out]

27:59.135 --> 28:00.512
[in Korean] Iblis went to meet who?

28:01.304 --> 28:02.514
[Irem] Jinniya.

28:02.597 --> 28:04.391
They must have met by now.

28:04.474 --> 28:06.184
He asked me where she was.

28:06.267 --> 28:08.603
Your arrogance could reach the heavens.

28:09.229 --> 28:12.440
I've just returned from restraining
Zahara and what? Jinniya?

28:14.609 --> 28:17.070
-[gasping]
-[tense music playing]

28:18.822 --> 28:21.533
Since when have I let you act
without my permission?

28:22.158 --> 28:25.703
If the kindhearted Jinniya let anything
slip, he'll chase that lead for sure.

28:25.787 --> 28:28.164
Even if it means shaking down
every last brother!

28:28.248 --> 28:30.041
[straining] I have…

28:31.668 --> 28:32.669
wronged you.

28:32.752 --> 28:36.339
I blocked your ears so you would not hear,
yet you still chirped away.

28:36.965 --> 28:39.509
I shall take that voice
which says whatever it pleases.

28:41.094 --> 28:42.554
I trust you'll take good care

28:43.888 --> 28:45.515
of the one thing you have left.

28:46.599 --> 28:48.143
[whooshing]

28:51.563 --> 28:53.565
[tense music continues playing]

29:15.462 --> 29:17.088
Why do you keep following me?

29:17.714 --> 29:21.801
Master told me to protect you
just in case anything happens.

29:21.885 --> 29:24.095
He sure is watching me closely
in case I die.

29:24.179 --> 29:27.223
He has waited a thousand years,
so he must be biding his time.

29:28.600 --> 29:30.810
He's already had
his once-in-a-lifetime romance.

29:32.020 --> 29:33.438
What caused the breakup anyway?

29:33.521 --> 29:35.440
So you figured it out?

29:35.523 --> 29:36.483
Irem dumped me.

29:36.566 --> 29:40.570
What's with the sudden confession?
I was asking about Iblis and Jinniya.

29:40.653 --> 29:42.864
Right, them. So you saw.

29:42.947 --> 29:46.159
With them, too,
my master was dumped by Jinniya.

29:46.826 --> 29:48.578
-Why?
-I thought you saw her.

29:48.661 --> 29:52.457
Jinniya is incredibly beautiful.
My master really doesn't measure up.

29:55.168 --> 29:58.838
About all the wiper fluid you drank.
I'll have to dock it from your pay.

29:59.839 --> 30:00.840
All of a sudden?

30:01.341 --> 30:03.343
[pleasant music playing]

30:10.141 --> 30:11.476
-[Min-ji chuckles]
-[clicks]

30:11.559 --> 30:12.393
[giggles]

30:14.312 --> 30:15.313
Ah!

30:18.817 --> 30:20.777
[Mi-ju] Goodness me,
how much gold is this?

30:22.946 --> 30:24.113
Over there. That way!

30:24.739 --> 30:25.573
[exclaims]

30:27.951 --> 30:30.119
[Min-ji] I guess you don't know much
about it.

30:30.203 --> 30:32.080
That sort of illness can't be cured.

30:33.915 --> 30:37.752
She always takes her medication.
She even sets reminders to take them.

30:37.836 --> 30:41.047
[Min-ji] They're just sleeping pills
and a sort of craving suppressant.

30:41.130 --> 30:44.342
The rest is basically candy
to put her grandma at ease.

30:44.843 --> 30:46.886
-Don't tell her grandma though.
-[sighs softly]

30:49.597 --> 30:52.308
I guess she has a lot of secrets.

30:52.892 --> 30:53.726
Mi-ju?

30:54.227 --> 30:56.145
That look on your face is a big no.

30:57.730 --> 31:00.608
She may not have any emotions,
but she's totally amazing.

31:00.692 --> 31:02.902
The meds are just a helping hand.

31:03.403 --> 31:05.864
Is that so? That's right. You're right.

31:05.947 --> 31:08.575
Whose words would I believe, if not yours?

31:08.658 --> 31:10.869
You're my dear Ka-young's best friend. Mm.

31:10.952 --> 31:14.455
So stop concerning yourself
with other women, and focus on me.

31:16.374 --> 31:19.544
I'm tall,
so I've never bought heels before.

31:20.628 --> 31:22.213
Should I buy these or not?

31:22.297 --> 31:26.259
[gasps] The shoe has found its way
to its true owner.

31:26.968 --> 31:29.429
Then absolutely buy them.
I'll get them for you. Huh?

31:29.512 --> 31:30.847
[in English] Excuse me.

31:30.930 --> 31:33.057
[in Korean] Can we get these? We'll--

31:33.141 --> 31:35.935
You must be out of your mind.
Do you know how much these cost?

31:36.019 --> 31:39.689
-You should be stopping me.
-Why? Just wear them out.

31:39.772 --> 31:43.693
I have a ton of money. I'm super rich
from trading stocks, you know.

31:44.903 --> 31:46.613
I just want to buy you something.

31:48.448 --> 31:49.532
Okay?

31:53.453 --> 31:58.291
[tour guide] This blade here is called
Muttalib's Sword or Iblis's Rage.

31:58.374 --> 32:02.337
According to legend, Muttalib,
the outsider, stole Iblis's treasure,

32:02.420 --> 32:06.215
and Iblis, enraged,
struck this sword down as a warning.

32:06.299 --> 32:08.593
No one has been able
to remove it since then,

32:08.676 --> 32:13.556
so when developing this city,
they created a square and built around it.

32:17.101 --> 32:19.354
[slow somber music plays]

32:31.074 --> 32:33.242
Why is Shaytan…

32:34.410 --> 32:36.746
Leisurely sightseeing, are we?

32:36.829 --> 32:38.539
What? No.

32:41.834 --> 32:44.629
Uh, I heard you went to the desert,
so I went for a walk.

32:47.256 --> 32:48.800
So is that really your rage?

32:49.300 --> 32:50.176
What is?

32:52.553 --> 32:55.056
-Hmm?
-[man straining]

32:59.769 --> 33:01.896
What the… Why is that there?

33:09.028 --> 33:11.155
[curious mystical music plays]

33:14.325 --> 33:16.786
So this sword really is your rage?

33:16.869 --> 33:19.080
Rage might be a bit of a stretch.

33:20.915 --> 33:24.002
But it is my sword.
Wait, so why is it stuck in here?

33:26.129 --> 33:28.840
-Uh--
-What? It really is mine.

33:28.923 --> 33:30.633
Maybe I got drunk and left it

33:31.759 --> 33:32.677
here?

33:33.720 --> 33:35.179
That happened every so often.

33:35.763 --> 33:36.848
Put it back. Now.

33:36.931 --> 33:38.558
-Mm?
-It's a tourist site now.

33:38.641 --> 33:40.768
And that's a rule. One of Dubai's rules!

33:40.852 --> 33:42.520
I was just putting it back.

33:43.438 --> 33:46.274
I only carried it around to show off
in the Middle Ages.

33:46.983 --> 33:50.153
Seeing how much people like it
does make me feel proud.

33:51.654 --> 33:54.699
I guess I'll just leave it
until I figure out why it's here.

34:02.957 --> 34:04.083
[strains]

34:04.709 --> 34:06.878
-Didn't I just move it?
-[tour guide] Sure. Who's next?

34:06.961 --> 34:09.380
You don't even have 1,000 won.
What was your treasure?

34:09.464 --> 34:12.175
The tea set your ex bought you?
Or the rug your ex--

34:12.258 --> 34:16.095
That reminds me.
Who was that woman we saw at the airport?

34:16.929 --> 34:18.347
I've been itching to know.

34:18.431 --> 34:22.435
Her? Min-ji's ex-girlfriend.
Like someone else, her ex-girlfriend.

34:22.518 --> 34:24.395
Right. [laughs]

34:24.479 --> 34:27.273
So that's why they exchanged
such longing looks.

34:27.356 --> 34:30.860
So, ex-girlfriends are to be longed for?
Did you long for Jinniya too?

34:30.943 --> 34:33.154
Why do we keep talking in circles?

34:35.156 --> 34:37.867
Wait, then why was Min-ji's ex
glaring at you?

34:38.409 --> 34:40.495
Who knows? She was always that way.

34:43.206 --> 34:44.749
[woman] We're having gamja-tang again?

34:45.374 --> 34:49.045
-Do you even know what today is?
-Of course I do. Our 300-day anniversary.

34:49.629 --> 34:50.755
I'm sorry.

34:51.339 --> 34:53.299
But I already made these plans.

34:53.382 --> 34:54.842
-[clatters]
-I'm done with this.

34:54.926 --> 34:58.346
Of the thousands of dishes out there,
why does it have to be gamja-tang?

34:58.930 --> 35:01.891
Not many dishes let you enjoy
the marrow in each joint.

35:01.974 --> 35:04.310
Would you just shut up
so the two of us can talk?

35:04.393 --> 35:05.853
[sucking]

35:06.562 --> 35:09.482
Choi Min-ji. I can't take this anymore.
Choose. Is it her or me?

35:11.192 --> 35:12.235
Leave.

35:14.028 --> 35:15.363
I loved you.

35:16.280 --> 35:17.115
[scoffs]

35:18.783 --> 35:21.953
Fine. Have a great life or whatever.

35:26.707 --> 35:28.793
She wished you well. Why the tears?

35:29.418 --> 35:32.672
-Just see her. See her and see me too.
-[sighs]

35:33.881 --> 35:36.551
That's just not possible. [sighs]

35:39.971 --> 35:40.805
[sighs]

35:40.888 --> 35:43.474
[Sade] Wow, what a heartbreaking story.

35:43.975 --> 35:47.353
I've got a one-sided crush too, actually.

35:47.854 --> 35:49.605
She has a cute, fluffy coat--

35:49.689 --> 35:51.023
No one asked you.

35:52.233 --> 35:55.236
Where should we go today?
Today's our last day here.

35:55.903 --> 35:58.906
Ka-young said we had somewhere to go,
just the two of us.

35:59.657 --> 36:01.701
The two of you? Why? Where?

36:02.869 --> 36:03.744
Mm.

36:05.413 --> 36:06.664
My goodness.

36:09.208 --> 36:10.668
Ka-young!

36:11.294 --> 36:13.754
Hey, come and help me apply this.

36:14.922 --> 36:16.632
Here. [sighs heavily]

36:17.425 --> 36:20.261
I told you to ditch pain relief patches
and see a doctor.

36:20.761 --> 36:22.513
These work like a charm.

36:22.597 --> 36:25.933
If I see a doctor,
they'll just tell me to get surgery.

36:26.017 --> 36:27.935
No way am I letting a knife near me.

36:28.019 --> 36:30.479
It's my dream to be
in the Miss Korea pageant.

36:30.563 --> 36:32.940
And you never know,
I might still have a shot.

36:33.441 --> 36:37.195
My mom made a huge fuss
when I got married.

36:37.278 --> 36:41.490
She was saying I should be hitting salons
in Myeong-dong, not getting married.

36:41.574 --> 36:45.036
-Should I be laughing? [dryly] Ha-ha.
-[chuckling]

36:47.997 --> 36:50.541
Grandma, do you miss Mom?

36:51.042 --> 36:52.043
Mom?

36:52.668 --> 36:55.922
Of course I miss her. That's a given.

36:57.048 --> 37:00.343
She passed away
less than a year after I got married.

37:00.426 --> 37:02.386
No, not your mom, my mom.

37:05.848 --> 37:06.849
Your daughter.

37:08.601 --> 37:09.644
Right.

37:12.021 --> 37:13.147
Well, I…

37:14.649 --> 37:16.234
I do think about her.

37:16.817 --> 37:17.693
But

37:18.402 --> 37:21.113
she hasn't even visited
in 20 years, so, well…

37:23.532 --> 37:24.659
That damn girl.

37:25.993 --> 37:27.036
So you do miss her.

37:28.079 --> 37:31.082
[poignant music playing]

37:33.793 --> 37:35.836
[breath trembling]

37:40.508 --> 37:44.637
My goodness. Goodness me.

37:47.139 --> 37:50.184
[crying softly]

38:18.504 --> 38:21.590
Mom had a far better mom
than she deserved.

38:24.677 --> 38:25.928
How infuriating.

38:27.346 --> 38:29.223
[watch ticking]

38:29.307 --> 38:32.393
[poignant music continues playing]

38:37.231 --> 38:39.275
[cries softly]

38:39.859 --> 38:41.319
[banging loudly]

38:41.402 --> 38:43.029
Hey, you psycho bitch!

38:43.112 --> 38:45.448
Just go ahead and make your wish first!

38:47.366 --> 38:48.743
CLOSED TODAY

38:48.826 --> 38:52.038
You really think I'll make mine first
just because you're holding out?

38:52.121 --> 38:55.416
You have no fucking idea
how much of an opportunity this is!

38:56.417 --> 38:57.293
Hey!

38:59.545 --> 39:01.172
[Bo-gyeong screaming]

39:02.089 --> 39:04.008
[Bo-gyeong continues screaming]

39:09.597 --> 39:11.307
Mom, are you divorcing Dad?

39:11.390 --> 39:13.768
First you get fired, and now this?

39:14.268 --> 39:17.271
You get out too.
You said you wanted to live alone.

39:17.355 --> 39:19.732
Really? You're getting me my own place?

39:19.815 --> 39:21.650
What, do I owe you a place?

39:22.151 --> 39:25.112
You're on your own from now on.
I could just not give birth to you.

39:25.196 --> 39:28.866
What are you talking about?
Are you saying you regret having me?

39:29.575 --> 39:31.869
So you can resent me,
but I can't resent you?

39:33.287 --> 39:34.789
You made me regret it, damn it!

39:35.831 --> 39:37.458
I gave you two chances,

39:37.541 --> 39:40.628
and you still managed
to screw everything up!

39:42.380 --> 39:44.507
[breath trembling]

39:48.928 --> 39:51.680
[tense music playing]

39:52.640 --> 39:53.891
So this is your final wish.

39:56.894 --> 39:58.020
It is.

39:59.397 --> 40:00.898
My final wish…

40:07.363 --> 40:09.448
is for you to forget

40:10.449 --> 40:11.992
I already made two wishes.

40:12.993 --> 40:14.453
[sighs, tuts]

40:16.956 --> 40:18.541
Alas, the greed of humans.

40:32.138 --> 40:33.264
It's been fulfilled.

40:33.848 --> 40:36.350
[chuckles in relief] Really?

40:40.146 --> 40:42.857
Humans always end up
falling into this trap.

40:44.066 --> 40:44.984
Think about it.

40:45.067 --> 40:48.362
If the wish that man made
after 72 years had actually worked,

40:49.905 --> 40:52.533
would I have remembered that story
and told it to you?

40:54.493 --> 40:55.411
What?

40:56.745 --> 40:58.747
[tense music continues playing]

41:06.755 --> 41:09.842
-[ringing]
-[whooshing]

41:13.637 --> 41:14.805
[Im-seon gasps]

41:15.806 --> 41:18.392
KANG IM-SEON, AUGUST 2, 2024
MADE HER FINAL…

41:21.562 --> 41:22.521
I guess

41:23.355 --> 41:24.273
I'm going to lose.

41:25.691 --> 41:28.152
Not yet. That's just one person.

41:28.736 --> 41:30.154
We have the mutt and YouTuber.

41:30.237 --> 41:33.657
But Eom Sang-tae and Gu Bo-gyeong
are already a done deal.

41:35.117 --> 41:36.160
Listen carefully.

41:36.744 --> 41:39.872
You still have one final wish.
You can just undo all of this.

41:39.955 --> 41:40.998
Just wish for it.

41:41.081 --> 41:42.208
I can't do that.

41:42.291 --> 41:44.502
If I do, I can't catch Eom Sang-tae, and…

41:47.671 --> 41:48.547
you would lose.

41:53.511 --> 41:58.724
[clears throat] By the way, does everyone
give up so easily after the three wishes?

41:59.225 --> 42:00.726
Don't they say, "Just one more"?

42:09.360 --> 42:11.612
So their memories disappear.

42:14.031 --> 42:15.908
The moment their final wish is granted,

42:16.492 --> 42:20.371
they forget who they met,
what they lost in order to gain something,

42:21.038 --> 42:23.666
and everything related to you.

42:24.959 --> 42:25.793
Is that right?

42:32.299 --> 42:33.342
Does that mean…

42:36.720 --> 42:37.555
I will too?

42:39.306 --> 42:41.809
[soft ballad playing]

42:49.650 --> 42:50.943
But will you

42:52.403 --> 42:53.654
remember me?

42:56.782 --> 42:57.783
Yes.

43:14.466 --> 43:15.718
That's not very fair.

43:33.986 --> 43:36.614
[soft ballad continues playing]

44:27.289 --> 44:29.500
-[birds chirping]
-[ducks quacking]

44:33.420 --> 44:36.256
[birds continue quacking
and chirping]

44:45.557 --> 44:46.767
I visited Dubai.

44:46.850 --> 44:47.976
It's a necklace.

44:51.522 --> 44:52.481
Of all things?

44:53.107 --> 44:54.525
What's with the sign language?

44:55.192 --> 44:57.027
Wait, your neck. Were you hurt?

44:57.111 --> 44:59.446
Don't tell me he took your voice too?

44:59.530 --> 45:02.408
Damn that Ejllael!
I won't just let this slide!

45:02.491 --> 45:05.285
Hey! Are you insane? Get back here!

45:06.036 --> 45:07.162
[inaudible]

45:08.914 --> 45:12.501
-[growling]
-Let go. Let go of me, damn it!

45:13.544 --> 45:16.046
[Sade] Ejllael, you're evil!

45:16.130 --> 45:18.340
Just let go! Come on!

45:18.841 --> 45:20.926
[Sade] Ejllael, you're evil!

45:21.009 --> 45:23.095
[Iblis] What the hell is going on here?

45:23.178 --> 45:25.514
How dare you lay your hands
on a mythical beast!

45:26.014 --> 45:28.267
-This beast of yours bit me first!
-[cries]

45:28.350 --> 45:31.103
Take him right now and piss off,
or I'll obliterate him!

45:31.186 --> 45:34.273
All right. I'll take him
and piss off for you.

45:38.068 --> 45:44.783
[screams] How far are you throwing me?

45:45.742 --> 45:47.744
[upbeat pop music playing]

45:48.912 --> 45:50.122
[exhales]

45:58.714 --> 45:59.882
[distorted groaning]

46:05.554 --> 46:07.681
[distorted groaning]

46:20.486 --> 46:21.320
Wow.

46:22.446 --> 46:23.697
[yells]

46:25.032 --> 46:26.283
[distorted groaning]

46:28.577 --> 46:31.330
[distorted groaning]

46:47.095 --> 46:50.849
[panting] Hey. Let's stop. I'm wiped out.

46:50.933 --> 46:52.559
[panting] Fine.

46:53.936 --> 46:54.978
Just answer me this.

46:55.562 --> 46:57.314
You said I stole one of your feathers

46:58.482 --> 47:00.317
before I was locked up, didn't you?

47:01.401 --> 47:02.778
What exactly did I do

47:04.029 --> 47:04.947
with that feather?

47:05.030 --> 47:07.616
How the hell would I know that?

47:07.699 --> 47:09.201
At least tell me when it was.

47:09.701 --> 47:11.745
How long before I was locked up?

47:12.246 --> 47:13.455
[pants]

47:13.539 --> 47:15.249
I've got a 20-year hole in my memory.

47:15.332 --> 47:18.335
[both panting]

47:19.711 --> 47:21.547
Who said that? Did Jinniya say that?

47:23.590 --> 47:26.093
Wait, you're that bitch from back then.

47:27.386 --> 47:29.263
So you all know something.

47:30.806 --> 47:33.809
Fine. For now,
just take the life of that immortal.

47:34.393 --> 47:37.396
He'll come after Ki Ka-young
because she broke the thread.

47:37.479 --> 47:40.232
[scoffs] How would I do that?

47:41.024 --> 47:43.277
You're overlooking three things.

47:43.360 --> 47:46.238
First. Even I can't take the life
of an immortal.

47:46.321 --> 47:48.615
Just how would I go about
revoking your magic?

47:48.699 --> 47:50.909
Second. The immortal
isn't after Ki Ka-young.

47:50.993 --> 47:52.452
He's after you.

47:52.536 --> 47:54.496
He wants to become your master.

47:56.790 --> 47:57.958
And third.

47:58.542 --> 47:59.751
I told you this already.

47:59.835 --> 48:01.545
Shadi is not a hostage.

48:03.714 --> 48:04.923
That immortal…

48:07.092 --> 48:08.677
is actually Shadi's son.

48:08.760 --> 48:10.929
[suspenseful music plays]

48:11.013 --> 48:12.014
His son?

48:17.269 --> 48:19.229
But I heard Shadi's son was dead.

48:25.110 --> 48:27.529
[suspenseful music playing]

48:41.251 --> 48:43.920
[panting]

49:03.523 --> 49:04.608
[Jun-u] Aren't you scared?

49:06.735 --> 49:10.197
-[panting]
-Do you go hiking often?

49:10.280 --> 49:11.114
No.

49:11.615 --> 49:12.783
This is my first time.

49:13.408 --> 49:15.452
Rough trail though. It almost killed me.

49:15.952 --> 49:17.746
Either way, it's good to see you.

49:22.542 --> 49:25.295
[tense music playing]

49:25.379 --> 49:26.380
Ka-young.

49:27.798 --> 49:29.549
How many wishes do you have left?

49:33.720 --> 49:36.056
I thought it was particularly quiet today.

49:37.140 --> 49:39.518
Move. You're not the one
really asking that question.

49:39.601 --> 49:40.519
So you're aware.

49:41.812 --> 49:43.772
But, you see, I don't know a thing.

49:43.855 --> 49:46.066
So please just give me a straight answer.

49:46.733 --> 49:48.360
They want me to ask you that.

49:49.069 --> 49:50.696
Those guys are terrifying.

49:51.279 --> 49:52.614
They even kill people.

49:53.615 --> 49:56.159
The moment I answer that question,
I'll die anyway.

49:56.910 --> 49:59.204
And my loved ones
would be in danger again.

50:00.497 --> 50:01.415
Is that right?

50:05.377 --> 50:07.629
It's just that I've racked up some debt.

50:08.588 --> 50:10.674
So I just need to do
what I was sent to do.

50:13.468 --> 50:15.387
I was told to do this
if you didn't answer.

50:16.680 --> 50:18.056
I mean it when I say

50:19.182 --> 50:20.767
this is nothing personal.

50:21.601 --> 50:24.146
-[gasps]
-[music intensifies]

50:25.939 --> 50:26.940
[gasps]

50:31.278 --> 50:36.491
The auto shop. The cars I fix.
My adjustable wrench. Frogs.

50:39.953 --> 50:43.331
-The sound of dental scaling. Gamja-tang.
-[laughs]

50:43.415 --> 50:45.667
-[Ka-young] Min-ji.
-[watch ticking]

50:45.751 --> 50:47.794
-[Ka-young] Grandma.
-[chuckles]

50:48.628 --> 50:52.799
[Pan-geum] "I will now also
give you sorrow."

50:54.050 --> 50:55.385
Lee Mi-ju.

50:58.972 --> 51:00.807
Kki Kka-young.

51:00.891 --> 51:03.477
I just need 1,000 won.
Ki Ka-young. Ki Ka-young!

51:04.269 --> 51:07.272
[Ka-young] I'm taking care of you now.
I can't do this if I lose.

51:09.608 --> 51:10.984
[gasps]

51:27.584 --> 51:30.170
What do you think you're doing?
Do you really want to die?

51:31.713 --> 51:34.716
So this is what they call fear. [pants]

51:35.842 --> 51:37.719
Fear is really scary.

51:39.721 --> 51:41.640
But I didn't fall on purpose.

51:42.307 --> 51:43.975
Then you should've made a wish.

51:44.059 --> 51:45.685
A wish to be saved!

51:46.895 --> 51:47.854
You almost died.

51:47.938 --> 51:49.731
If I made my final wish…

51:55.362 --> 51:56.613
I'd forget you.

51:57.864 --> 51:59.866
[touching music playing]

52:08.875 --> 52:10.961
You damn psychopath!

52:17.592 --> 52:21.054
[romantic ballad playing]
